# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the checkout platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf would otherwise hand
# entrypoint.sh to the Linux container with CRLF line endings. The kernel then
# reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r" and the container dies with
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory" -- a failure that only appears
# inside Docker and never locally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the Dockerfiles' RUN lines and for compose/env files that
# get sourced inside containers.
DockerFile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
